# The ported old Electron renderer's inventory, now at `app/lib/` — the IPC
# shim, the locale loader and the pure `*-core` modules the shell reaches
# through `@lib/*`.
#
# Still unformatted, still on purpose. These 76 files are a VERBATIM port
# (single quotes, no semicolons, the old app's house style), and a reformat is
# a whole-file diff on every one of them. Put under the move it would have made
# PR B unreadable — a reviewer could no longer see that not one line changed;
# put here on its own it is a 12 000-line commit that says nothing.
#
# So it happens FILE BY FILE, when a file is opened for a real reason: take it
# out of this ignore, format it, tighten it to `app/`'s ESLint rules (see the
# `app/lib/**` block in eslint.config.js), in the same PR as the change that
# made you open it. The day the list is empty, both lines go.
app/lib

# `legacy/` is what the inventory left behind: the ts-rs `bindings/` (generated
# code is never reformatted), the seven locale catalogues, `types/` and
# `shared/` — all verbatim port or generated output, same reasoning as above.
legacy

# ts-rs bindings: src/lib/bindings is the transient regen target; the committed
# copy lives at legacy/bindings (already covered by the `legacy` entry above).
src/lib/bindings

# The atlas (Fase A, «Frivilligen først»): PNGs plus two markdown reports that
# `npm run atlas` wrote. The photographer itself was deleted in fase B with the
# shell it photographed; these files stay as the historical record and are
# generated output, so they are not format-gated. docs/design/ATLAS.md is
# hand-written and stays covered.
docs/design/atlas
